  "findings": [
    "Metadata and Create-only authentication set actual job owner to approved alias; Send-only authentication preserves original owner",
    "Create-only login after durable journal begin plus lost Create acknowledgement leaves actual alias-owned held job with original-user record, job ID unknown, no Send and no automatic retirement; metadata-auth control cancels owned job",
    "Send-only worker forwards one unauthenticated Send and receives explicit401; callback approves credentials but no authenticated Send is issued. Job remains incoming, record retains correct original owner, automatic cleanup refuses changed account",
    "Source confirms cupsFinishDestDocument calls cupsGetResponse; the latter authenticates/reconnects on401 and returns NULL without resending the document. Explicit401 differs from lost/ambiguous acceptance and must never enable blind retry"
  ],
  "primary_sources": [
    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OpenPrinting/cups/v2.4.20/scheduler/ipp.c",
    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OpenPrinting/cups/v2.4.20/cups/dest-job.c",
    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/OpenPrinting/cups/v2.4.20/cups/request.c",
    "https://openprinting.github.io/cups/doc/policies.html"
  ],
  "remaining": "Fix with regression tests at real worker/journal/HTTP seams; explicit protected recovery and held-job authentication remain separate required behavior"
